🔥 Backpropagation in PyTorch

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

📌 Autograd System

PyTorch automatically computes gradients using **autograd**.

---

Example Code

```python id="p1"
import torch

sample data
x = torch.tensor([[1.0]], requires_grad=True)
y_true = torch.tensor([[2.0]])

parameters
w = torch.tensor([[0.5]], requires_grad=True)
b = torch.tensor([[0.0]], requires_grad=True)

forward pass
y_pred = x @ w + b
loss = (y_true - y_pred)**2

backward pass
loss.backward()

gradients
print(w.grad, b.grad)

update weights
with torch.no_grad():
    w -= 0.01 * w.grad
    b -= 0.01 * b.grad

    w.grad.zero_()
    b.grad.zero_()
```

---

🧠 Key Points

✔ `.backward()` computes gradients
✔ `.grad` stores gradients
✔ Use `torch.no_grad()` for updates

